  "body": "Running bullet or bulletfarm without arguments opens the operator TUI. Keep navigation and detach responsive during credential discovery, display validated operator records without waiting for command discovery, and add Fleet, Ready Queue and Outbox panes with actual server identities. Improve midnight/cyan/amber rendering, ANSI/NO_COLOR fallback, persistent shortcuts and operator help.\n\nBind authenticated reads and command/revoke mutations to the expected session acknowledgement before consuming responses. Keep submission records separate from execution rows and preserve exact reconnect subjects. Retain fail-closed execution admission while reconciling earlier proposals.\n\nValidation on f73a657: complete canonical local required passed 1,280 selected fast tests, 34 contract tests, five additional preservation tests, lint, security and docs. All seven hosted required checks passed. The installed developer binary from product commit d9b1ace passed both-alias PTY startup/help/palette/detach checks; actual native Tuiwright passed all 12 scenarios. Later changes affect fixtures, CI policy and documentation. Terminal tests reserve capacity while retaining six concurrent clients per scenario and existing deadlines. Historical failed runs remain preserved; excluded host-dependent cases receive no passing credit.\n\nThe durable task composer, executing Head, supervised native provider sessions and signed installed service remain incomplete. This branch conflicts with main and needs reviewed reconciliation plus independent approval. Component UI evidence is not live-provider or release acceptance.\n",
